---
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro';

const lastUpdated = 'September 2026';

// Products that customers can pay for. Each has its own terms, which sit on
// top of these and win where they differ.
const products = [
  { name: 'SSLBoard', href: 'https://sslboard.com/terms-conditions/', site: 'sslboard.com' },
  { name: 'quickS3', href: 'https://quicks3.com/terms/', site: 'quicks3.com' },
];
---

<Layout
  title="Terms and Conditions"
  description="The terms that apply to every Gone Coding Ltd. product, including SSLBoard and quickS3."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-16">
    <header class="space-y-4">
      <p class="font-mono text-[13px] text-muted-foreground">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">Terms and Conditions</h1>
      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
        These terms apply to every product and website operated by Gone Coding Ltd. Each paid
        product also has its own terms, which cover how that product works.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="mt-12 space-y-10 leading-relaxed">
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">1. Who we are</h2>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground">
          Gone Coding Ltd. is a company registered in Hong Kong, at Unit 1603, The L. Plaza,
          367-375 Queen's Road Central, Sheung Wan, Hong Kong. In these terms, "we", "us" and
          "our" mean Gone Coding Ltd., and "you" means the person or organisation using our
          products.
        </p>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground">
          You can reach us at <a class="underline decoration-primary/60 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-primary" href="mailto:contact@gone-coding.com">contact@gone-coding.com</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">2. These terms and product terms</h2>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground">
          Each paid product has its own terms, which form part of your agreement with us:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc space-y-1 pl-6 text-muted-foreground">
          {products.map((product) => (
            <li>
              <a class="underline decoration-primary/60 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-primary" href={product.href}>
                {product.name} terms
              </a>{' '}
              ({product.site})
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground">
          Where a product's own terms say something different from these terms, the product terms
          apply for that product. By creating an account or paying for a product, you accept these
          terms and that product's terms.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">3. Business use</h2>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground">
          Our paid products are sold to businesses for business use. By subscribing you confirm
          that you are acting for a business and not as a consumer, and that the person accepting
          these terms is authorised to do so on that business's behalf.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">4. Your account</h2>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground">
          You are responsible for what happens under your account, for keeping sign-in details
          safe, and for the people you invite into it. Tell us promptly if you believe an account
          has been used without permission.
        </p>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground">
          You are responsible for any credentials, keys or systems you connect to a product, and
          for making sure you are allowed to connect them.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">5. Acceptable use</h2>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground">You agree not to:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc space-y-1 pl-6 text-muted-foreground">
          <li>break any law that applies to you or to us, including data protection and export rules</li>
          <li>use a product against systems, domains or storage you do not own or have permission to use</li>
          <li>interfere with a product's operation, security or availability, or work around its limits</li>
          <li>resell or make a product available to others except as its own terms allow</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">6. Fees, billing and taxes</h2>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground">
          Prices are shown on each product's website. Subscriptions are billed in advance for the
          period stated there, and payments are processed by Stripe. We do not see or store your
          full card details. Each product's terms set out what you are billed for, such as the
          number of users, and how changes during a period are handled.
        </p>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground">
          Prices exclude any taxes you are responsible for, including taxes due under a reverse
          charge mechanism. All fees are non-refundable unless the product's terms say otherwise or
          the law requires otherwise. We may change prices with at least 30 days' notice to
          existing subscribers.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">7. Trials</h2>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground">
          Where a product offers a free trial, its length and what happens when it ends are set out
          in that product's terms. We may change or withdraw trials for new customers at any time.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">8. Cancellation, suspension and termination</h2>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground">
          You can cancel a subscription at any time, and cancellation takes effect as described in
          the product's terms. If payment fails or a subscription ends, access may be restricted or
          suspended as those terms describe.
        </p>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground">
          We may suspend or end access if you break these terms, if we are required to by law, or
          to protect the security of a product or its other users. We aim to give notice where we
          reasonably can.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">9. Your data and connected systems</h2>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground">
          You keep ownership of your data and of anything you store in systems you connect to a
          product. You grant us the rights needed to operate the product for you, such as
          processing and transmitting that data. Each product's documentation and privacy policy
          describe what it accesses and for how long records are kept. Our <a class="underline decoration-primary/60 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-primary" href="/privacy-policy/">privacy policy</a> explains how we handle personal data.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">10. Our intellectual property</h2>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground">
          The products, their software, interfaces and content are owned by us or our licensors.
          These terms give you a limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable right to use them while
          your subscription is active. You may not copy, modify, reverse engineer or create
          derivative works from them except where the law allows it.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">11. Third-party services</h2>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground">
          Our products work with services run by other companies, such as storage providers,
          certificate authorities and payment processors. We are not responsible for those
          services, their availability, or the fees they charge you directly.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">12. Service levels and changes</h2>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground">
          We work to keep our products available and accurate, but we do not promise uninterrupted
          or error-free service unless a product's terms say so. We may change, add or remove
          features. Where a change materially reduces what you have paid for, we will tell you.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">13. Disclaimer</h2>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground">
          To the extent the law allows, our products are provided "as is" and "as available",
          without warranties of any kind, whether express or implied, including any implied
          warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, or non-infringement.
          Reports, scans and other output are informational, and you remain responsible for
          decisions you make based on them.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">14. Liability</h2>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground">
          To the extent the law allows, we are not liable for indirect, incidental, special or
          consequential losses, or for lost profits, revenue, goodwill or data. Our total liability
          arising out of or relating to a product is limited to the fees you paid us for that
          product in the 12 months before the event giving rise to the claim.
        </p>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground">
          Nothing in these terms excludes liability that cannot be excluded by law.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">15. Indemnity</h2>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground">
          You agree to indemnify us against claims, losses and reasonable costs arising from your
          use of a product, your breach of these terms, or your infringement of someone else's
          rights.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">16. Changes to these terms</h2>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground">
          We may update these terms. If a change materially affects you, we will give notice by
          email or in the product before it takes effect. Continuing to use a product after that
          means you accept the updated terms.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">17. Governing law</h2>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground">
          These terms are governed by the laws of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region, and
          the courts of Hong Kong have exclusive jurisdiction, unless a product's own terms provide
          otherwise.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">18. Contact</h2>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground">
          Questions about these terms: <a class="underline decoration-primary/60 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-primary" href="mailto:contact@gone-coding.com">contact@gone-coding.com</a>.
          For help with a specific product, write to its own support address: <a class="underline decoration-primary/60 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-primary" href="mailto:contact@sslboard.com">contact@sslboard.com</a> or <a class="underline decoration-primary/60 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-primary" href="mailto:contact@quicks3.com">contact@quicks3.com</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
